* =====================================================================================================
* sleep_current__rt9080.lib -- RT9080-33GJ5 3.3 V LDO, DC model for the sleep-current budget (.op only)
*
* Part      : Richtek RT9080-33GJ5 (main board U1)
* Datasheet : https://www.richtek.com/assets/product_file/RT9080/DS9080-09.pdf  (DS9080-09, December 2024)
*
* Modelled (all at the DC operating point):
*   VOUT     3.3 V nominal, tracks VIN when VIN < 3.3 V (dropout), smooth min() with 1 mV knee
*   RPASS    0.52 ohm series pass resistance = VDROP 0.31 V typ / 600 mA (EC table, "3 V <= VOUT")
*   IQ       2 uA typ / 4 uA max, ILOAD = 0, VIN >= VOUT + VDROP  (EC table "Quiescent Current")
*   KGND     optional ground-current slope vs load (A/A). 0 by default (IQ only). The only light-load data
*            is the "Ground Current vs. Load Current" plot (VIN 4.3 V, VOUT 3.3 V), which starts at 1 mA
*            where IGND is about 58 uA (25 C; 53-65 uA over -40..65 C); the chord to IQ gives KGND = 0.056.
*            The test uses it only as a sensitivity case: IGND below 1 mA load is NOT specified.
*   Current conservation: the output current is drawn from VIN (F source), so the battery sees it.
*   MAXC = 0 typical, 1 datasheet maximum (IQ only).
*
* NOT modelled: IQ vs temperature (no curve in DS9080-09), ground current in dropout (VIN < 3.3 V, not
*   specified), line/load regulation, VOUT accuracy (+-2 %), output discharge (EN is tied to VIN), dynamics.
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt SC_RT9080 vin en vss vout params: MAXC=0 KGND=0
.param iq = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 4u : 2u}
.param vnom = 3.3
.param rpass = 0.52
* EN rising threshold 0.9 V (EC table VEN_R); EN is tied to VIN on this board, so this only gates ship mode
Eout vx vss vol = '((vnom + v(vin,vss) - sqrt((vnom - v(vin,vss))**2 + 1e-6))/2) * (v(en,vss) > 0.9 ? 1 : 0)'
Rpass vx vy {rpass}
Vsns vy vout 0
Fin vin vss Vsns 1
Bgnd vin vss I = '(v(en,vss) > 0.9 ? 1 : 0) * (iq + KGND * max(i(Vsns), 0))'
.ends SC_RT9080
